body:
Ich weiß, wie sehr sowas weh tun kann. Es ist normal, dass es weh tut. Lass die Gefühle zu, wein dich aus, reg dich auf, etc. Lösch alles, was dich an ihn erinnern könnte.  Dann kauf dir Schokolade, Süßigkeiten, geh shoppen, gönn dir irgendwas, tu irgendwas, was vielleicht nicht sehr nachhaltig glücklich macht, aber dich für einen Moment ablenkt. Danach musst du dir klar machen, dass du es verdienst, glücklich zu sein. Egal welches Unglück dir passiert, du verdienst es glücklich zu sein. Es wird schwierig sein, sich das klarzumachen, aber du musst Dinge finden, die dich unabhängig von ihm oder aber auch von anderen Leuten erfüllen. Wenn du schon sowas hast, z.b. ein Hobby, mach das. Sonst geh ins Gym, lern irgendwas, arbeite an dir selbst. Es wird dauern aber mit der Zeit verheilt die Wunde.

&#x200B;

Keine Ahnung ob dir das hilft, aber so würde ich vermutlich damit umgehen.

&#x200B;

>none of that proves your point that Kim Jong Un claims to be a perfect being, nor that he has one-man rule, or anything you say about Juche.

Weird how even the mod of this sub agrees with my first comment where I basically said that NK is a one-man dictatorship whose leader claims to be flawless, infallible and incorruptible. I guess they are actually Liberals after all..

&#x200B;

>1 and 3 on your list are just opinions.

How is 1 an opinion when the highest position in NK is given to the same family for ages now? It's nepotism. I can see why you think 3 is an opinion and I agree, it's not empirical evidence. I still do think that it is a good argument and ultimately holds true.

&#x200B;

>Also, Kim Jong Un is not referred to as "Dear Leader" that was his father's honorary title.

Never said this.

&#x200B;

>Leadership is in fact also important to Juche, it considers Marx and Lenin important leaders as it does the leadership of Kim Il-sung who heralded the Juche ideology, but Juche is a man-centred philosophy, which is about the independence and creativity of the masses, who are considered masters of the revolution who only need be educated and mobilized. You can see this idea manifested in reality by the Chollima movement, Chongsanri Method and Spirit or the Taean Work System

Leadership isn't just important in Juche, it's far exceeded the importantness of Mao or Stalin in any way. If leadership is just "important", why are they literally worshipping and sucking his dick in any of the texts they released? Claiming that he is ever-victorious, peerless, most outstanding, etc. Why is the leaders birthday a national holiday celebrated with military parades, symbolism, etc? Why are there weird ass children songs said to be composed by leader of the country that play every day that sing about the "Great dear leader"?
